.github
# [MANTLE] The build context is the whole checkout, and mantle-config's build
# workflow (mantle-app-build-only-qa.yaml) checks it out with full history and
# `submodules: recursive` by default, so without these the daemon receives
# ~2.7GB that no build step reads.
#
# .git also makes `COPY . .` unstable: FETCH_HEAD and logs/ differ on every
# checkout, so the layer hash changes even when no source file did, and every
# layer after it is rebuilt.
#
# Verified before excluding:
#   - no build.rs reads git metadata (three are `build_all()`; bindings/build.rs
#     needs forge, which the image does not have, and skips); `vergen` /
#     `vergen-git2` are not depended on by any member
#   - contracts/src stays: validity/src/relay_rejection.rs `include_str!`s
#     OPSuccinctL2OutputOracle.sol. It is under #[cfg(test)] and the image
#     builds binaries only, but src/ is 32K so keeping it costs nothing and
#     leaves `cargo test` working inside the image
#   - elf/ stays: utils/elfs `include_bytes!`s both committed ELFs
#   - validity/migrations, migrations-rollback and .sqlx stay (not excluded)
#   - tests/ is Go e2e only; nothing in the Rust build reads it
.git
/contracts/lib
/contracts/out
/contracts/cache
/tests
